{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAncestors"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q: those parents lie in the answer’s subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. So a query is one range minimum over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 parent positions (the Euler tour reduction on half the entries), answered by 64-entry"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"blocks with a bitmask of each prefix’s minimum stack and a sparse table over the blocks’ minima."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"About two words per vertex, plus (n\/64)·log₂(n\/64) for the table."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/lowestcommonancestors"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/LowestCommonAncestors"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TreeAlgorithms"}],"ro